\section{Methods}

\subsection{Overview of the MPS--PCE Architecture}

The Multiscale Pathology Simulation \& Precision Countermeasure Engine
(MPS--PCE) is a modular, mechanistic simulation framework designed to model
divergent pathological etiologies across four decoupled computational modules:
\[
\mathcal{M} = \{\mathcal{M}_A,\, \mathcal{M}_B,\, \mathcal{M}_C,\, \mathcal{M}_D\},
\]
corresponding respectively to genetic dysregulation, pathogen kinetics,
acute biomechanical trauma, and cellular aging/senescence. Each module
operates under independent mechanistic assumptions and is parameterized
directly from clinical diagnostic vectors.

