\subsubsection{Senescence Module ($\mathcal{M}_D$)}
Cellular aging is modeled using senescent cell fraction $s(t)$:
\[
\frac{ds}{dt} =
\rho(\Theta_D) - \gamma(\Theta_D) s(t).
\]

\subsection{Simulation Execution}

The full system trajectory is generated by:
\[
\hat{\mathbf{\Omega}}(t)
=
\mathcal{F}_{\Theta}\big(
\mathbf{\Omega}_0,\,
\mathbf{U}(t)
\big),
\]
where $\mathbf{U}(t)$ denotes the therapeutic countermeasure vector.
Numerical integration is performed using adaptive Runge--Kutta--Fehlberg (RK45)
methods with stiff--system detection. Biological non--negativity constraints
are enforced via projection:
\[
\Pi_{\ge 0}(x) = \max(x, 0).
\]

\subsection{Monte Carlo Replication}

For each patient, $N = 10{,}000$ Monte Carlo trajectories are generated:
\[
\big\{\hat{\mathbf{\Omega}}^{(n)}(t)\big\}_{n=1}^{N},
\]
to estimate predictive uncertainty and countermeasure robustness.

\subsection{Error Metrics and Statistical Validation}

Predictive fidelity is quantified using Normalized Mean Absolute Error (NMAE):
\[
\text{NMAE}
=
\frac{1}{N}
\sum_{i=1}^{N}
\frac{
\left|
\hat{\mathbf{\Omega}}_i(t)
-
\mathbf{\Omega}_{\text{true},i}(t)
\right|
}{
\bar{\mathbf{\Omega}}_{\text{true},i}
}.
\]

Hypothesis testing is performed using paired t--tests:
\[
H_0:\;
\text{MPS--PCE predictive error is indistinguishable from baseline models}
\]
\[
H_1:\;
\text{MPS--PCE predictive error is significantly lower}.
\]

Bayesian posterior likelihoods are computed as:
\[
p\big(
\mathbf{\Omega}_{\text{true}}
\mid
\Theta
\big)
=
\mathcal{N}
\Big(
\hat{\mathbf{\Omega}}(t),
\boldsymbol{\Sigma}
\Big),
\]
where $\boldsymbol{\Sigma}$ encodes laboratory assay noise.

